{"uid":"6e57133e65ac68ec","name":"test_no_adjudication_episode_starts_at_an_already_expired_boundary[deadline]","fullName":"tests.test_midrun_adjudication_episode#test_no_adjudication_episode_starts_at_an_already_expired_boundary","historyId":"de7875a1a29522b997806fb201531817","time":{"start":1791881298112,"stop":1791881298141,"duration":29},"description":"Task cure-01-01-2 (v0.24 requirement A.1/B.3, DoD 1-3, #169): this\n    episode is a bare async call from inside `_step_worker`'s own `while\n    self.budget_left():` loop BODY, so the loop's own boundary check (only\n    re-consulted at the top of the next turn) does not stand between a\n    worker iteration that just spent the last of the budget/deadline and\n    this call -- exactly the `review_edges.py::test_petition_\n    adjudication_does_not_start_after_deadline` reproduction this task\n    cures, now driven through the SAME real `_step_worker` path and\n    `_worker_supervisor` fixture the ordinary in-budget test above uses\n    (canonical run-side open petition, task already `awaiting-\n    validation`, so `_maybe_run_midrun_adjudication_episode` is reached\n    from the `pending_verify` branch, strictly after the worker\n    iteration that expires the boundary INSIDE itself).\n\n    An already-expired boundary must start NO new adjudication review\n    iteration; the petition stays open (unsettled, eligible again after\n    an operator resume -- `_petition_adjudication_seen` is never touched\n    by the early return); and the pass still lands in the shared\n    `timed_out`/null-verdict freeze path (task 010/011's C.1 path), never\n    a second freeze implementation of its own.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task cure-01-01-2 (v0.24 requirement A.1/B.3, DoD 1-3, #169): this<br />\nepisode is a bare async call from inside <code>_step_worker</code>'s own <code>while self.budget_left():</code> loop BODY, so the loop's own boundary check (only<br />\nre-consulted at the top of the next turn) does not stand between a<br />\nworker iteration that just spent the last of the budget/deadline and<br />\nthis call -- exactly the <code>review_edges.py::test_petition_ adjudication_does_not_start_after_deadline</code> reproduction this task<br />\ncures, now driven through the SAME real <code>_step_worker</code> path and<br />\n<code>_worker_supervisor</code> fixture the ordinary in-budget test above uses<br />\n(canonical run-side open petition, task already <code>awaiting- validation</code>, so <code>_maybe_run_midrun_adjudication_episode</code> is reached<br />\nfrom the <code>pending_verify</code> branch, strictly after the worker<br />\niteration that expires the boundary INSIDE itself).</p>\n<pre><code>An already-expired boundary must start NO new adjudication review\niteration; the petition stays open (unsettled, eligible again after\nan operator resume -- `_petition_adjudication_seen` is never touched\nby the early return); and the pass still lands in the shared\n`timed_out`/null-verdict freeze path (task 010/011's C.1 path), never\na second freeze implementation of its own.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791880795037,"stop":1791880795037,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791880795038,"stop":1791880795038,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791881298084,"stop":1791881298085,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent"